---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How Relicbound Works"
  description="Choose a nearby expedition, complete the walk and recover relics for your museum."
>
  <section class="page-header">
    <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
    <h1>Turn an ordinary walk into an expedition.</h1>
    <p class="introduction">
      Relicbound removes the difficult part of deciding where to walk, then
      rewards the completed route with discoveries for a persistent museum.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="steps" aria-label="Relicbound game loop">
    <article>
      <span>01</span>
      <h2>Choose your time</h2>
      <p>
        Select a Quick, Standard, Long or Extended Expedition based on how
        much time you have available.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article>
      <span>02</span>
      <h2>Compare destinations</h2>
      <p>
        Relicbound searches for nearby points of interest and checks that
        Apple Maps can provide a pedestrian route.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article>
      <span>03</span>
      <h2>Complete the walk</h2>
      <p>
        Follow walking directions while Relicbound records the active
        expedition, including distance and duration.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article>
      <span>04</span>
      <h2>Recover sealed cases</h2>
      <p>
        Completed expeditions award between one and four cases. Longer walks
        recover more cases.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article>
      <span>05</span>
      <h2>Build your museum</h2>
      <p>
        Discover 105 relics from four lost civilisations, increase your museum
        rank and complete each collection.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article>
      <span>06</span>
      <h2>Restore damaged relics</h2>
      <p>
        Duplicate discoveries become Restoration Fragments, which improve
        relic condition and reveal additional archive lore.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="privacy">
    <p class="eyebrow">Designed around privacy</p>
    <h2>Your expeditions remain on your device.</h2>
    <p>
      Relicbound requires no account and does not upload your walking history.
      Detailed GPS trails are not retained after an expedition.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-header {
    max-width: 52rem;
    margin-bottom: clamp(4rem, 10vw, 7rem);
  }

  .eyebrow {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    color: var(--colour-accent-bright);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  h1 {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .introduction {
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 2vw, 1.3rem);
  }

  .steps {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1px;
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid var(--colour-border);
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
    background: var(--colour-border);
  }

  article {
    min-height: 18rem;
    padding: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
    background: var(--colour-surface);
  }

  article span {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
    color: var(--colour-accent);
    font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  article h2 {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3vw, 2.25rem);
  }

  article p {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .privacy {
    margin-top: clamp(4rem, 10vw, 7rem);
    padding: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem);
    border: 1px solid var(--colour-border);
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
    background: var(--colour-surface);
  }

  .privacy h2 {
    max-width: 15ch;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .privacy p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  @media (max-width: 42rem) {
    .steps {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    article {
      min-height: auto;
    }

    article span {
      margin-bottom: 2rem;
    }
  }
</style>